.TH WERKMEISTER-BUDGET 1 "" "werkmeister" "Werkmeister Manual"
.SH NAME
werkmeister\-budget \- The scheduler's budget, the slots held and the features Waiting for room
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBwerkmeister budget\fR [command]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Shows the scheduler's budget and who is using it: the memory and CPUs a feature's containers may take in total (\fBbudget:\fR in \fB~/.werkmeister/config.yaml\fR, else the Docker engine's memory less 1 GiB and every CPU), the host\-load ceiling \fBwith\-temp\-home\fR, and a start that runs a setup service, wait under (not on macOS), whether a start that doesn't fit may stop features whose session is idle or waiting on a person (and a person's \fBfeature up\fR a working autonomous one), the features holding a slot, each \fBRunning\fR feature with the CPUs and memory it holds, its session state (idle, waiting on a person, working, a person's workspace) and whether a gate is running, and the features \fBWaiting\fR for room in admission order (gate starts first), each with what it waits to start, what that costs, and how long it has waited.
.PP
It reads only: with the host daemon up it asks the daemon for the queue, otherwise it reads \fB~/.werkmeister/scheduler/\fR itself.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
werkmeister budget status
werkmeister budget status \-\-json
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBwerkmeister\fR(1)
